  "title": "Donguibogam",
  "summary": "The Donguibogam, a 25-volume encyclopaedia of medical knowledge and treatment, was compiled in Korea and edited by the court physician Heo Jun on royal instruction; its original edition appeared in 1613. UNESCO says it developed ideals of preventive medicine and public health care by the state, and inscribed it on the Memory of the World Register in 2009.",
